WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.690
In English, it's a red car.

2
00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:05.720
In French, it's «une voiture rouge».

3
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.620
Word for word: a car red.

4
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.950
Simple rule? Not quite.

5
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.000
Sometimes moving one
word changes the meaning.

6
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.650
«mon cher ami» is my dear friend.

7
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:20.620
But «un pull cher» is an expensive jumper.

8
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.960
So why does French put the
adjective after the noun?

9
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.870
And when does the order flip?

10
00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:30.000
In this mission, you'll watch
adjective chips jump behind the noun.

11
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.440
Then you'll build phrases chip by chip,

12
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.870
and decide where each word sits.

13
00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.220
Your mission: work out
where French adjectives sit,

14
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.710
and when the order flips.
